@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+## Context
+
+`price()` in `src/index.ts` is shared by `quote` and `book`; it parses both times with `parseUtc`, which requires midnight UTC, then computes `dailyPrice * days`. Bookings store `start`/`end` in ms and overlap-check on them, so exact-hour periods already conflict correctly with each other and with whole-day bookings.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- **Optional `hourlyPrice` on `Equipment`**, validated like `dailyPrice` (non-negative safe integer) only when present (`undefined` means none). Anything else, such as `null`, a fraction or a negative, throws. It is stored with the item.
+- **Period parsing**: split the strict UTC format check from the midnight check. `price()` requires start and end to be on the hour (minutes, seconds, milliseconds zero). If `end - start < DAY_MS` the rental is hourly; otherwise it must also be at midnight on both ends, as today (so 24h or more from a non-midnight time throws). A midnight-to-midnight 24-hour period is one whole day, priced daily.
+- **Hourly pricing**: `hourlyPrice * hours`, no discount (always under 3 days). Throws if the item has no `hourlyPrice`. The safe-integer check applies as for daily.
+- **Crossing midnight is allowed** (e.g. 22:00 to 02:00), as it is shorter than a day.
+- **`availability` keeps requiring midnight periods** (unchanged contract); extending it is out of scope.
+- Only TypeScript and the Node standard library; no dependency.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Callers cannot yet ask which items are free for an hourly slot; `book` still rejects clashes.
+- The error for a non-midnight period of a day or more stays "must be at midnight UTC".
