@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+## Why
+
+Many visitors only want a board for an afternoon, and the desk has to turn them away because rentals are whole days only. Customers should be able to rent by the hour.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- `addEquipment` accepts an optional `hourlyPrice`: the cost of one hour of rental, a non-negative integer number of euro cents.
+- A rental shorter than a day (less than 24 hours) whose `start` and `end` are both on the hour is priced at the item's hourly price times the number of hours.
+- An item without an hourly price cannot be rented by the hour: `quote` and `book` throw for it.
+- Whole-day rentals (midnight to midnight UTC) are unchanged, including the 10% discount from 3 days.
+- Assumptions (see design): an hourly period may cross midnight; a period of exactly 24 hours or more must still be whole days; the long-rental discount does not apply to hourly rentals (they are always under a day); `availability` is unchanged.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+None.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- `rental`: Equipment registration (optional `hourlyPrice`), the period requirement (hourly periods), and Quote (hourly pricing). Booking totals like a quote, and overlap checks already work on exact times.
+
+## Impact
+
+- Affects rentals (quotes and bookings) for students and visitors alike. Lessons and customers are not affected.
+- Code: `src/index.ts`; tests in `test/rental.test.ts`.
+- No runtime dependency is introduced.
+
+## Scope
+
+In scope: optional `hourlyPrice` on equipment; hourly quotes and bookings for periods shorter than a day on exact hours.
+
+Out of scope: hourly-aware `availability` (it still takes whole-day periods), minimum hours, season or opening-hours limits, hourly discounts, per-customer-kind pricing, cancellations.
